						"dir": "auto"
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Now we have a cluster, but who is responsible for managing the cluster? where is the information about the members of the cluster stored? How are nodes monitored? When a node fails, how do you move the workload of the failed node to another worker node? That's where the master comes in. The  master is another node with kubernetes installed in it and is configured as a master. The master watches over the nodes in the cluster and is responsible for the actual orchestration of containers on the worker nodes."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
