			"index": "b0yHNU",
			"typeName": "shape"
		},
		{
			"x": 982.5234375,
			"y": 1314.89453125,
			"rotation": 0,
			"isLocked": false,
			"opacity": 1,
			"meta": {},
			"id": "shape:QBlHdHEvVZFlowdfxSKf_",
			"type": "text",
			"props": {
				"color": "black",
				"size": "s",
				"w": 91.3984375,
				"font": "draw",
				"textAlign": "start",
				"autoSize": true,
				"scale": 1,
				"richText": {
					"type": "doc",
					"attrs": {
						"dir": "auto"
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Container"
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
			"index": "ayzYa",
			"typeName": "shape"
		},
		{
			"x": -30.578125,
			"y": 96.65625,
			"rotation": 0,
			"isLocked": false,
			"opacity": 1,
			"meta": {},
			"id": "shape:Ec9q1Q65ge0b3ocb2MvlD",
			"type": "text",
			"props": {
				"color": "black",
				"size": "s",
				"w": 1452.8515625,
				"font": "draw",
				"textAlign": "start",
				"autoSize": false,
				"scale": 1,
				"richText": {
					"type": "doc",
					"attrs": {
						"dir": "auto"
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Kubernetes, also known as K8's, was built by Google based on their experience running containers in production. It is now an open source project and is arguably one of the best and most popular container orchestration technologies out there. In this lecture, we will try to understand kubernetes at a high level. To understand kubernetes we must first understand two things"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "orderedList",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto",
								"start": 1,
								"type": null
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "listItem",
									"attrs": {
										"dir": "auto"
									},
									"content": [
										{
											"type": "paragraph",
											"attrs": {
												"dir": "auto"
											},
											"content": [
												{
													"type": "text",
													"text": "Container"
												}
											]
										}
									]
								},
								{
									"type": "listItem",
									"attrs": {
										"dir": "auto"
									},
									"content": [
										{
											"type": "paragraph",
											"attrs": {
												"dir": "auto"
											},
											"content": [
												{
													"type": "text",
													"text": "Orchestration"
												}
											]
										}
									]
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Once we get familiarized with both of these terms, we would be in a position to understand what kubernetes is capable of."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"marks": [
										{
											"type": "code"
										}
									],
									"text": "Containers"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"marks": [
										{
											"type": "code"
										}
									],
									"text": "Need for Containers"
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "we will look at the most popular container available today which is Docker. I had this requirement to set up and end to end application stack, including various different technologies like a web server using node.js and a database such as MongoDB, and a messaging system like Redis, and an orchestration tool like Ansible. We had a lot of issues developing this application stack with all these different components. First of all, their compatability with the underlying OS was an issue. we had to ensure that all these different services were compatible with the version of OS we were planning to use. There have been times when certain versions of these services were not compatible with the OS, and we have had to go back and look at different OS that was compatible  with all of these different services. Secondly, we had to check the compatibility between these services and the libraries and dependencies on the OS. We have had issues where one service requires one version of a dependent library, whereas another service requires another version. The architecture of our application changed over time. We have had to upgrade to newer versions of these components or changge the database, etc. and every time something changed, we had to go through this same process of checking compatibility between these various components and the underlying infrastrucute This compatibility matrix issue is usually referred to as the matrix from hell."
								}
							]
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							}
						},
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Next, every time we had anew developer on board, we found it really difficult to set up a new environment. The new developers had to follow a large set of instructions and that run hundreds of commands to finally setup their environments. They had to make sure they were using the right operating system, the right versions of each components, and each developers had to set all that up by himself each time. we also had different developmet, test, and production environments. One developer may be comfortable using one OS, and the others may be comfortable using another one, and so we couldn't guarantee that the application that we were building would run the same way in different environments. And so all of this made our life in developing, building and shipping the application really difficult. "
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
			"index": "a2EAU",
			"typeName": "shape"
		},
		{
			"x": 546.0952337130726,
			"y": 2670.244630767301,
			"rotation": 0,
			"isLocked": false,
			"opacity": 1,
			"meta": {},
			"id": "shape:ql1KKaGHz0zllLoPgxIte",
			"type": "text",
			"props": {
				"color": "black",
				"size": "s",
				"w": 247.85157437984435,
				"font": "draw",
				"textAlign": "start",
				"autoSize": false,
				"scale": 1,
				"richText": {
					"type": "doc",
					"attrs": {
						"dir": "auto"
					},
					"content": [
						{
							"type": "paragraph",
							"attrs": {
								"dir": "auto"
							},
							"content": [
								{
									"type": "text",
									"text": "Kubernetes, aruguably the most popular of it all, is a bit difficult to setup and get started, but provides a lot of options to customize deployments and supports deployment of complex architectures."
								}
							]
						}
					]
				}
			},
			"parentId": "page:page",
			"index": "b0atrU",
			"typeName": "shape"
